{
  "id": "dual-process-theory",
  "term": "dual process theory",
  "definition": "Dual process theory is a framework for understanding choice and other mental activity by distinguishing between two broad kinds of processing: fast, intuitive, low-effort processing and slower, more deliberate, effortful processing. It also recognizes that real decision making can involve a combination of these two kinds of processes.",
